  "resources": {
    "costumbres": {
      "c-023cbca4b280a16e": {
        "fuente": {
          "entradaId": "freeman-80",
          "modulo": "freeman-manners-customs"
        },
        "texto": "He made him to ride in the second chariot which he had; and they cried before him, Bow the knee."
      },
      "c-03884fbfe62b5de7": {
        "fuente": {
          "entradaId": "freeman-79",
          "modulo": "freeman-manners-customs"
        },
        "texto": "For description of other kinds of seals see note on 1 Kings 21:8 (#323)."
      },
      "c-239faf19735f70a1": {
        "fuente": {
          "entradaId": "freeman-77",
          "modulo": "freeman-manners-customs"
        },
        "texto": "Contrary to the custom of the Hebrews and other Orientals, the Egyptians shaved closely, only allowing the beard to grow as a sign of mourning; thus reversing the custom of the Hebrews, who shaved as a token of mourning. See note on Isaiah 15:2 (#494). Strange to say, the Egyptia…"
      },
      "c-280b06894a2e6151": {
        "fuente": {
          "entradaId": "freeman-81",
          "modulo": "freeman-manners-customs"
        },
        "texto": "Granaries were often very extensive in Egypt, and every facility was made for the housing and subsequent delivery of the grain. The monuments have many illustrations of the different styles of store-houses that were in use, by which we can obtain some idea of the manner in which…"
      },
      "c-2c93b1a9d8a61830": {
        "fuente": {
          "entradaId": "freeman-78",
          "modulo": "freeman-manners-customs"
        },
        "texto": "This elevation of a slave to a position of high office, though uncommon among Western nations, was not so rare in the East. There, change of fortune was so sudden that the beggar of today might be the noble of tomorrow. Many of the most prominent characters in Oriental history we…"
      },
      "c-2f779a551cf0f1b8": {
        "fuente": {
          "entradaId": "freeman-76",
          "modulo": "freeman-manners-customs"
        },
        "texto": "These magicians (chartummim) were an order of Egyptian priests who understood the sacred hieroglyphic writings. They cultivated a knowledge of art and science, interpreted dreams, practiced soothsaying and divination, and were supposed to possess secret arts. They were men of gre…"
      }
    },
